    "title": "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"
  },
  "question": {
    ":question/id": "3636b04e-3417-5188-b715-30fde51f2ace",
    ":question/problem": "If $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix that has $2$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince $A$ has $4$ columns and $2$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n4-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
